KG42.register("rules-f5b523a8c6becb5c3ee0c0e8",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R006","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"An agent assigned the consumer role is restricted to that operating role. Scope: Consumer participants in the two-bus MBED application. Condition: Under the base formulation assigning each negotiating agent a producer or consumer role.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Consumer participants in the two-bus MBED application.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X001","symbol":"P_{nm}","meaning":"Bilateral traded quantity (net injection) of negotiating agent n with neighboring agent m under the MBED injection convention; for an agent assigned the consumer role, this quantity is constrained to be nonpositive.","kind":"operational","domain":"real (source gives D=(p_n in R^{|omega_n|})_{n in Omega} for the agent decision vector)","unit":null,"indices":["n","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e17"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"An agent assigned the consumer role is restricted to that operating role. Scope: Consumer participants in the two-bus MBED application. Condition: Under the base formulation assigning each negotiating agent a producer or consumer role.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Under the base formulation assigning each negotiating agent a producer or consumer role, a consumer agent's bilateral decision variables are sign-constrained to be nonpositive: P_nm \u003c= 0 for every n in the consumer set Omega_c and every neighboring agent m in omega_n.","expression":"P_{nm} \\le 0 \\quad \\forall (n,m) \\in (\\Omega_c, \\omega_n)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e17"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"m- The power set-points of an agent n are constrained by the ny power boundaries Pn and Pn, ms a Pn ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The role of each agent is restrained to either producer or consumer (P_n P̄_n ≥ 0) as it simplifies the following derivations. Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e26","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"IV-A. Simulation Setup","anchor_text":"is e- A. Simulation Setup ly p- The setup is composed of 12 agents: 6 producers includ- ta ing two w","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"IV. APPLICATION AND CASE STUDIES\n... A. Simulation Setup\n    The setup is composed of 12 agents: 6 producers includ-ing two wind turbines, 2 solar PV and 2 fossil generators and 6 consumers including 4 household consumers and 2 industrial consumers. The sequences of wind and solar PV production are taken from [20] and [21]. The consumption sequences as well as the ﬂexibility capacity are derived from [21]. The non time-varying market participants are taken from [5]. Note that compared to [5], non-zero lower boundary con-straints have been added for the generators. The capacities of the generators and consumers are adapted to be comparable. It was chosen to model the PV and the wind turbines as must-take generators (Pn = Pn). This allow do deﬁne for them a virtual cost function (an and bn) without affecting the optimal solution."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e27","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":"1000","section":"IV-A. Simulation Setup","anchor_text":"buses. cost function (an and bn) without affecting the optimal solution. Another option would be to ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The trades are differentiated through a single criterion (cnm =\ncnγnm) that aims at increasing self and local consumption. For\nthat purpose γnm  is chosen to be the euclidean distance be-\ntween agents n and m. The agents are split into two buses (see\nFig. 3), with 3 generators and 3 loads each. Note that the MBED\nmodel can be operated without a corresponding network layer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e17","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"II-C. MBED Formulation","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK Pnm + Pmn = 0 ∀(n, m) ∈(Ω, ω","equation_id":"(9c), (9d), (9e)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P_nm + P_mn = 0 ∀(n, m) ∈ (Ω, ω_n) (9c) P_nm ≥ 0 ∀(n, m) ∈ (Ω_p, ω_n) (9d) P_nm ≤ 0 ∀(n, m) ∈ (Ω_c, ω_n) (9e) where D = (p_n ∈ R^{|ω_n|})_{n∈Ω}. Ω_p and Ω_c are the sets of producers and consumers, respectively."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"This rule's source-supported formal content is a role/sign restriction on the bilateral trading variable; it introduces no numeric fixed parameters. Power-boundary parameters Punderline_n and Pbar_n appear in the surrounding MBED formulation but are not declared here because the frozen graph for this rule exposes only the consumer-role node and the supplied evidence does not resolve their overline/underline notation in this scope."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"The role of each agent is restrained to either producer or consumer"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e26","quote":"6 consumers including 4 household consumers and 2 industrial consumers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e27","quote":"The agents are split into two buses (see Fig. 3), with 3 generators and 3 loads each."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"c0bf0c87303e23c6dba0474349c184469429778a318e8bcd689cc2e82c36ca3d","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The rule has a source-supported mathematical sign restriction on consumer bilateral trades. C001 is preserved as the procedural role-assignment constraint. C002 transcribes the consumer sign condition in v141-b-g01-e07 and v141-b-g01-e17: P_nm \u003c= 0 for n in Omega_c and m in omega_n. A variable P_nm is declared because the sign restriction operates on that bilateral trade variable. The product role-exclusivity condition P_n Pbar_n >= 0 is not formalized due to unresolved overline/underline notation in the supplied evidence; see revision_requests. Evidence remains unreviewed under this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-X001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P_{nm} is the bilateral trade quantity whose sign is determined by the consumer-role assignment; the only frozen node in this rule is participation.consumer, which anchors the participant side of this unary role restriction. No edge is available in the rule's frozen E."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The consumer sign constraint is a mathematical consequence of the agent being assigned the consumer role, so it is attached to participation.consumer. The frozen graph has E=[] for this rule, so no edge binding is used."}],"revision_requests":["If the role-exclusivity condition P_n Pbar_n >= 0 is required as a separate constraint, B re-extraction must resolve the overline/underline notation for the lower and upper power-boundary symbols Punderline_n and Pbar_n; the current rule evidence renders the product ambiguously.","If the unit of the bilateral traded quantity P_nm is required, B re-extraction must state it; the supplied evidence gives the real-domain decision vector but not a unit for this rule's scope."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
